+# R46 B7b R2 — independent Sol LOW prerequisite check
+
+LENS: closure of findings 1–5, honest preservation of finding 6, and bankability of the partial interface
+
+FINDINGS:
+
+1. `ggml/src/ggml-backend-impl.h:21,34`, `ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp:458,1068,19358,19234`, and `tests/test-backend-ops.cpp:13679-14063` | a prerequisite with finding 6 open must not claim whole-load semantics or obsolete fallback behavior | The shared contract and many implementation/test labels still call this “whole-load” planning even though the production boundary covers one `(buffer type, context)` group. The enum says INDETERMINATE means “allocate unplanned,” and the Vulkan return-site repeats that claim, while R2 now refuses an INDETERMINATE multi-buffer group before allocation. These comments make the partial API’s scope and status contract materially inaccurate. Rename the surface consistently to per-buffer-type/group planning and describe INDETERMINATE as caller-policy-dependent before banking it. | confidence: h
+
+CHECKED:
+
+1. Finding 1 is closed: current `reserve_plan()` contains the decrement/undo backtracking block at `ggml-vulkan.cpp:1197-1199`; no planted greedy return remains. Fresh `heapres` passes the backtracking and search-bound assertions.
+2. Finding 2 is closed: the live total-capacity condition is `if (need > free_total)` at `ggml-vulkan.cpp:1145`; no `&& false` remains. All six current hashes and the 1415-insertion/83-deletion diffstat match `16-hashes-and-diffstat.txt`.
+3. Finding 3 is closed honestly: Red D is withdrawn. Current-tree reds A, B, C, E, and F have the claimed nonzero receipts and named failures; Red E specifically returns rc 1 on `impossible load: DECIDED infeasible`, and Red F aborts at the caller assertion. Restoration hashes match current source bytes.
+4. Finding 4 is closed in code: `GGML_BACKEND_API_VERSION` is 3, and the dynamic loader rejects any unequal version before accessing a buffer-type object. In-tree registrations use the version macro; trailing aggregate fields zero-initialize for rebuilt non-planning backends. The focused ggml/llama targets and current narrow targets build successfully. The pre-existing `ggml-zdnn` version anomaly is unrelated and already rejected by the same equality gate.
+5. Finding 5 is closed: `ggml-alloc.c` refuses INDETERMINATE when `n_ranges > 1` before entering the allocation loop. The new backend-independent test proves zero allocation calls for that case, preserves one-buffer fallback, preserves UNSUPPORTED behavior, and exercises FEASIBLE/INFEASIBLE. Red F disables the guard and the test aborts.
+6. Finding 6 remains open and is accurately explained in `OPUS-R46-B7B-R2-REPORT.md:§7`: `llama_model::load_tensors()` still allocates each `ml.ctx_map` entry before planning the next. No cross-group loader transaction exists.
+7. Fresh narrow verification: `ninja -C build-vulkan test-alloc test-backend-ops`, `test-alloc.exe`, and `test-backend-ops.exe heapres` all returned rc 0. No model, inference, server, bench, performance, timing, bandwidth, or throughput run was performed.
+8. Bankability assessment: the implementation is a coherent and valuable per-buffer-type transaction prerequisite after the inaccurate contract labels are corrected. Reverting the behavior is not warranted; its atomic reservation, rollback, ABI gate, and caller policy are independently useful and form the needed substrate for the later cross-group loader owner.
+
+NOT CHECKABLE: True multi-device isolation and the no-maintenance4 path are not executable on this rig. The cross-group loader transaction is intentionally unimplemented.
+
+BLOCKED
