+1. `ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp:1194-1197` | deterministic complete/backtracking assignment | The current tree is left in planted-red A state: after the first dead end, `reserve_plan()` returns `VK_PLAN_INFEASIBLE` instead of undoing the prior choice and continuing. A fresh narrow rebuild succeeded, but `test-backend-ops.exe heapres` returned rc 1 with all four backtracking assertions and the search-bound assertion failing. | confidence: h
+2. `ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp:1145`, `r46b-b7b-evidence/24-revert-identity.txt`, and `OPUS-R46-B7B-WHOLE-LOAD-REPORT.md:§9` | final restoration and hashes must match the reviewed executable tree | The total-capacity precheck is also left disabled as `if (need > free_total && false)`. The current Vulkan source SHA-256 is `8f3e7a2447f3d84b3fad40d11eab4039b500f28e3c7c29f15acfe9d6de351325`, not the report's `74978f...`; the retained revert receipt only proves restoration to the earlier `74978f...` tree and does not cover the later changes. The report's diffstat is likewise stale (735/331 changed lines versus the current 780/384). | confidence: h
+3. `r46b-b7b-evidence/23-heapres-red-d.rc` and `23-heapres-red-d.txt` | planted reds must be real and receipt claims must match | Red D did not fire: its receipt is `rc=0` and its output ends `heapres: all tests passed`. This directly contradicts the report's table and prose claiming all four reds fired at rc 1, so the already-live-reservation negative proof is not discriminating as retained. | confidence: h
+4. `ggml/src/ggml-backend-impl.h:11,34-56` and `ggml/src/ggml-backend-reg.cpp:247` | ABI/interface initializer compatibility across all backends | Three fields were appended to `ggml_backend_buffer_type_i` while `GGML_BACKEND_API_VERSION` remained 2. Source rebuilds zero-initialize omitted trailing fields, but a dynamically loaded backend built against the old layout still advertises version 2 and can pass the registry gate; core code then reads `plan_begin` beyond the smaller old object. The report's claim that an old dynamic backend “still works” is not binary-safe. | confidence: h
+5. `ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp:1003-1011,1155-1157` and `ggml/src/ggml-alloc.c:1188-1267` | tri-state fallback cannot permit partial placement when complete feasibility is unknown | Hitting the search bound returns `INDETERMINATE`; `ggml-alloc.c` then uses the ordinary per-buffer allocator. That path may allocate part of the set before failing, which the report explicitly acknowledges. This does not provide the required whole-set guarantee for every plan input; the test even treats this partial-allocation fallback as required behavior. | confidence: h
+6. `src/llama-model.cpp:1748-1831` and `ggml/src/ggml-alloc.c:1168-1267` | the full intended model/load allocation set must be known and reserved before allocation | `llama_model::load_tensors()` loops over `ml.ctx_map` and calls `ggml_backend_alloc_ctx_tensors_from_buft()` separately for each buffer type; each completed call allocates before the next context is planned. The implementation therefore provides per-buffer-type transactions, not the requested whole model/load transaction grouped across all Vulkan allocations. The report labels this missing loop-level owner as B7c, although B7c was scoped to bounded host splitting/staging capacity. | confidence: h
+
+CHECKED:
+
+1. Inspected every changed file against accepted parent `a031ffef4c9bcaa2e61151856a2f6f76283632f5`: `ggml-alloc.c`, `ggml-backend-impl.h`, `ggml-backend.cpp`, `ggml-vulkan.cpp`, and `tests/test-backend-ops.cpp`.
+2. Verified the production call at `llama-model.cpp:1808`, the preceding `ml.ctx_map` loop, two-pass range collection, plan wrappers, Vulkan requirements/usage helpers, candidate type/heap separation, ledger-locked plan reservation, reservation adoption, rollback paths, and test seams.
+3. Read the compact B7b evidence only. Reds A-C have rc 1 with named failures; Red D has rc 0 and no failures. Production symbol census reports zero seam symbols in the non-test TU.
+4. Fresh narrow verification: `ninja -C build-vulkan test-backend-ops` returned rc 0; `build-vulkan/bin/test-backend-ops.exe heapres` returned rc 1 with five planner failures. No performance, model-load, inference, server, bench, timing, bandwidth, or throughput command was run.
+5. `git diff --check` is clean apart from the disclosed LF-to-CRLF warning for `tests/test-backend-ops.cpp`.
+
+NOT CHECKABLE: The no-maintenance4 runtime path and true multi-GPU isolation are unavailable on this rig. B7c host/staging capacity is outside this check.
+
+BLOCKED
