+## 3. Finding 4 — dynamic-backend layout compatibility
+
+The hazard is real: `ggml_backend_buffer_type` embeds `ggml_backend_buffer_type_i` **by value**, so a
+backend DSO built against the old layout allocates a smaller object, and core code reading
+`buft->iface.plan_begin` would read past it.
+
+The mechanism used is the one ggml already has for exactly this: `ggml-backend-reg.cpp:247` compares
+`reg->api_version` against `GGML_BACKEND_API_VERSION` for **strict equality** and refuses the DSO
+otherwise. `ggml/src/ggml-backend-impl.h:15` is bumped `2 → 3`. An old-layout dynamic backend is now
+unloadable, so the new layout can never be read off a smaller object. Source audit
+(`15-abi-version-audit.txt`):
+
+- every in-tree backend advertises the macro, never a literal `2` (13 call sites listed);
+- nothing in CMake, CI or docs pins `api_version == 2` — the only two occurrences of the identifier
+  outside backend registration are the gate itself and the struct field declaration;
+- pre-existing upstream anomaly, unchanged by this round: `ggml-zdnn` advertises `ZDNN_VERNUM`, not
+  `GGML_BACKEND_API_VERSION`. It was already unequal to 2 and is still unequal to 3.
+
+Trade-off, stated rather than hidden: this refuses *all* old dynamic backends, including ones that
+would otherwise have worked. That is the deliberate fail-closed choice — the alternative
+(`ggml_backend_reg_get_proc_address` negotiation with no struct growth) buys binary compatibility for
+old DSOs at the cost of an extra indirection layer around a boundary that §7 says is not final yet.
+If B7c or a later round keeps the plan hooks, revisiting that choice is cheap; interpreting an old
+struct with a new layout is not.
