+## 1. The production call chain
+
+CHECKED by reading the source, not assumed:
+
+```
+llama_model::load_tensors                       src/llama-model.cpp:1808
+  -> ggml_backend_alloc_ctx_tensors_from_buft   ggml/src/ggml-alloc.c:1239
+     -> ..._from_buft_impl                      ggml/src/ggml-alloc.c:1168
+        [ pass 1 ] split the context into the COMPLETE set of buffer ranges
+        [ NEW    ] ggml_backend_buft_plan_begin(buft, sizes, n, &status)
+        [ pass 2 ] per range: ggml_backend_buft_plan_alloc_buffer(buft, plan, i)
+                              (or ggml_backend_buft_alloc_buffer when unplanned)
+           -> ggml_backend_vk_buffer_type_plan_alloc_buffer
+              -> ggml_vk_create_buffer(..., planned)
+                 -> vkAllocateMemory
+        [ NEW    ] ggml_backend_buft_plan_free(buft, plan)   // releases every UNCONSUMED entry
+```
+
+`ggml_backend_alloc_ctx_tensors_from_buft_impl` is the earliest point where the complete intended
+allocation set is actually known: it already walked every tensor and computed every buffer boundary
+before it allocated the first buffer. It is not a new loader-global API — it has real production
+callers today, all of which now go through the plan path when the backend implements it:
+
+| Caller | Site |
+|---|---|
+| model weight load | `src/llama-model.cpp:1808` |
+| KV cache | `src/llama-kv-cache.cpp:645`, `:2505`, `src/llama-kv-cache-dsv4.cpp:985` |
+| recurrent memory | `src/llama-memory-recurrent.cpp:136` |
+| LoRA / adapters | `src/llama-adapter.cpp:82`, `:385` |
+| context memory buffers | `src/llama-context.cpp:3294` |
+| mtmd / clip | `tools/mtmd/clip.cpp:3601` |
+
+The negative tests in §6 drive this exact function; nothing is proved through a helper.
