+## 8. The next boundary — B7c
+
+B7c is **bounded host splitting with an explicit staging reserve**, and the concrete boundary is now
+visible from here:
+
+1. **Cross-buffer-type atomicity.** `llama_model::load_tensors` builds one `ggml_context` per buffer
+   type and calls `ggml_backend_alloc_ctx_tensors_from_buft` per type. To make a *whole model load*
+   one transaction, the plans for all of its buffer types must be opened before any of them
+   allocates — i.e. a plan set held across the loop in `llama-model.cpp`, released together. The
+   hooks added here are already the right shape for that; what is missing is the loop-level owner.
+2. **The staging reserve.** `device->sync_staging` and the prealloc scratch buffers are allocated
+   *after* the weights, as single-buffer callers. A bounded host split has to charge that staging
+   requirement into the same plan, otherwise a load can be declared feasible and then fail on the
+   staging buffer it needs to transfer into the buffers it just placed.
+3. **Host-side capacity.** This work charges Vulkan heaps only. Bounded host splitting needs a
+   second budget dimension (pinned host memory) in the same transaction.
+
+Minimal next patch: extend `plan_begin` to take a per-buffer-type *set* (or add a device-level plan
+that owns several buffer-type plans), and teach `ggml_vk_create_buffer_device`'s staging and prealloc
+paths to consume from it.
+
